{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Banking Ratios Toolkit: Analyse HDFC Bank FY2015–2024",
  "scenario": "You're a junior analyst on a Mumbai desk covering HDFC Bank. Your senior asks you to compute the five essential banking ratios (NIM, CASA, GNPA, CAR, ROA) across a decade of financials and identify which years signalled strength versus stress. This is how you move beyond standard leverage ratios to sector-specific insights.",
  "instructions": "Using the Data sheet with HDFC Bank's 10-year annual financials, compute NIM, CASA Ratio, GNPA Ratio, CAR, and ROA in the Answers sheet. Then identify the year with the highest NIM and flag whether rising GNPA ever signalled stress.",
  "learning_objective": "Compute Net Interest Margin, CASA Ratio, Gross NPA Ratio, Capital Adequacy Ratio, and ROA for a bank; then synthesise these five ratios to identify periods of profitability strength and asset-quality stress.",
  "hints": [
    "NIM = (Net Interest Income ÷ Average Interest-Earning Assets) × 100. CASA = (Current & Savings Deposits ÷ Total Deposits) × 100. Both are percentages.",
    "GNPA Ratio = (Gross NPAs ÷ Gross Advances) × 100. CAR = (Capital ÷ Risk-Weighted Assets) × 100. ROA = (Net Profit ÷ Average Total Assets) × 100.",
    "For 'Year with Highest NIM', use INDEX and MATCH on the NIM row; for 'GNPA Stress Flag', use an IF to check if any GNPA Ratio > 2%."
  ],
